KG42.register("clusters-4e334455a4bbd5a03b12fdaf",{"id":"37-dsm_auction_incentives::v142-d-CL002","paper":"37-dsm_auction_incentives","label":"Declaration-driven hourly configuration and consumption-period start-up","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"Declaration-driven hourly configuration and consumption-period start-up","market_meaning":"The distribution company selects a consumption configuration based on demand declarations; when the declared daily total is fixed, only the hourly distribution is adjusted and optimized according to supply cost. The configuration is used for billing, and after the configuration and payment obligation are set and announced, the corresponding consumption period is started.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","settlement","activation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The general welfare objective and the cost-minimization branch with a fixed daily total are retained separately; the reduction between them holds only under the stated conditions. R006 serves only as a shared interface for configuration billing and payment announcement, while the complete billing system belongs primarily to CL003; its Method 2 input cannot be extended unconditionally to Method 1.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The configuration decision, the handover from configuration to billing, and the announcement before consumption start-up have explicit informational and procedural connections and are suitable for assembly as a dispatch-implementation rule. The demand system belongs primarily to CL001, and the charging system belongs primarily to CL003; shared references are not counted as separate independent rules.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Responsible for configuration selection under the welfare objective, feasible scope and fixed-daily-total condition."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplies the procedural boundary that configuration completion and payment-obligation announcement precede consumption-period start-up."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides the per-user declaration entry point required for configuration; the information structures of the two methods continue to be retained separately."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Explains how the configuration enters billing and provides the amount interface for setting and announcing the payment obligation before start-up; the historical penalty system is handled by its primary cluster."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-C01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X005","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-T001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e004","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e011"],"rationale":"Per-user declarations according to the method used form the aggregated declaration-information input of the allocation rule. This is the interface from tuples to the configuration input for the user set; a single user tuple is not equated with the entire declared configuration, nor is the declared consumption vector equated with the optimization result."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-C02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x_i","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e29","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e011"],"rationale":"The (19) configuration branch with a fixed declared daily total corresponds to the configuration step completed before the start of the consumption period. R005 adds a procedural-timing meaning; reusing a configuration expression fragment does not constitute proof that two complete constraints are duplicated."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-C03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-VAR-x_i_s","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e008"],"rationale":"The hourly consumption term in (20) is taken from the corresponding vector component output by the configuration rule. This interface preserves the distinction between vector and component, and the cost-minimization interpretation is constrained by the fixed-daily-total condition."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-C04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-VAR-t_i","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C007"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e011","v141-b-g02-e012"],"rationale":"The payment rule provides the payment obligation that is set and announced before consumption begins; Table I makes clear that announcement precedes the start of consumption. This does not interpret the obligation announcement as the user having actually paid in advance, nor does it add a causal edge from the ordering."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R002::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R006::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e011"],"rationale":"The three places reference the same existing demand-submission node and respectively occupy the usage positions of declaration, configuration input and billing input; the presentation representation does not change these uses."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R005::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R006::V::clearing.social_welfare"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::clearing.social_welfare","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e011"],"rationale":"All three places reference the same configuration-decision node; the general welfare objective, conditional reduction and downstream use are still expressed by the respective original constraints."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R006::V::settlement.payment"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R006::V::settlement.payment","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e011","v141-b-g02-e012"],"rationale":"The billing node of R006 and the pre-start-up payment-obligation node of R005 are the same existing node; amount calculation and procedural timing are retained separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X001","v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x_i"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e011"],"rationale":"Only in the (19) branch for the same period, same user and fixed daily total do the two point to the same selected hourly configuration vector. The configuration-variable role of R002, the scheme-selection role of R005 and their scope differences are retained, and this is not extended to unconditional identity over the entire (18) scope."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-T001","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta_hat","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-PAR-theta_hat"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e008"],"rationale":"Limited to the Method 2 branch for the same period and the same user set, the three are the same aggregated declaration information used for configuration and billing. The parameter roles and general scope of each chain continue to be retained; this mapping does not cover Method 1 and does not resolve the hat-notation differences in the source text."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-M06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-C_s","v141-c-R006::theta::v141-c-R006-PAR-C_s"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g02-e001","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e008"],"rationale":"The (19) configuration objective and the (20) payment evaluation reuse the hourly supply-cost function of (2). The two function-parameter objects are retained in association according to their respective usage roles and are not rewritten into a new object."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"(19) requires preserving each user's declared daily total, but the frozen feasible set explicitly lists only hourly upper and lower limits and lacks the corresponding daily-total preservation condition. The existing feasible region is insufficient to close the reduction from (18) to (19).","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g01-e29","v141-b-g02-e007"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check whether the fixed daily total has another explicit feasible-region condition; C is to supply a sourced condition or indicate that the original text omits it; D does not add equations."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G02","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The relationship between the declared feasible region and the feasible region written in (18)/(19) is not clear, and the declared consumption vector cannot be directly regarded as the optimization result. On the same page, the two sets of B transcriptions of (19) differ in the hat notation of the declaration parameters.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X002","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X003","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X004","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-T001","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-T002","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-T003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e004","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g01-e29","v141-b-g02-e007"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the use of the true and declared feasible regions in configuration, the sources of the upper and lower limits, and the hat notation; upstream is to clarify the interface and retain the distinct identities of the declared quantity and the selected configuration quantity."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The frozen execution.energy_trade in this source carries the user's start of the consumption period; Table I refers only to a recommended consumption configuration and does not provide a basis for bilateral energy-exchange settlement or mandatory execution according to the plan.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e011","v141-b-g03-e15"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the semantic fit between the existing execution node and DSM consumption start-up, and propose an ontology revision separately if necessary; the current candidate covers only the start-up procedure and does not create transaction settlement or consumption-compliance constraints."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"The citations on which configuration, the payment interface and consumption start-up are based have still not undergone independent source verification; the conditional object associations are only candidate interpretations for this round.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e29","v141-b-g02-e001","v141-b-g02-e004","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e006","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e008","v141-b-g02-e011","v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g03-e15"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequent work is to check the original pages, formula conditions and procedure table item by item; maintain the unverified status and do not treat assembly relations as confirmation of scientific correctness."}]},"rule_refs":["37-dsm_auction_incentives::v141-c-R002","37-dsm_auction_incentives::v141-c-R005","37-dsm_auction_incentives::v141-c-R001","37-dsm_auction_incentives::v141-c-R006"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-20a5cdf8b3b1e9c9","COMP-8a2214d40b287af2","COMP-ebacec241379c91d","KG40-14a3066c15f25075"]});
